From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: Fix missing cleanup in error path

From: Samuel Holland
Acked-by: Paul Kocialkowski

Backported from linux-media: "[PATCH v2] media: cedrus: Fix missing cleanup in
error path", submitted by Andrey Skvortsov.  Carry it until it lands upstream,
then drop this patch.

v4l2_fh_init() must be paired with v4l2_fh_exit() before the containing
structure is freed.  cedrus_open()'s error path frees ctx without it.  No bug
is reachable today -- v4l2_fh_exit() only destroys an internal mutex -- but
that is a property of the current v4l2_fh, not a contract.

Origin: https://github.com/cstenger/allwinner-h713-mainline/blob/43b2cdd4aa1b161a281db8b10f02ce70085e2d42/patches/kernel/0113-media-cedrus-fix-missing-cleanup-in-error-path.patch (0113-media-cedrus-fix-missing-cleanup-in-error-path.patch, commit d5a4d98)
---
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
@@ -433,6 +433,7 @@
 err_m2m_release:
 	v4l2_m2m_ctx_release(ctx->fh.m2m_ctx);
 err_free:
+	v4l2_fh_exit(&ctx->fh);
 	kfree(ctx);
 	mutex_unlock(&dev->dev_mutex);
 
